@startuml shape-summary-derivation
' ============================================================================
' CurrentShapeSummaryV1::successor (semantic.rs:318-423, task 11943): the
' successor's shape summary from the predecessor's summary, the mutation batch
' and the rewrite report, without walking the successor state.
' Theory: formal/rocq/stack_safe_pda/theories/ExactStateShapeSummary.v
'   BLUE   #1565C0  the summary's totals and the inputs
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  the key-length multiset (a copy-on-write PathMap<u64>)
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  the derived successor summary
'   RED    #C62828  refusals
'   GREY   #607D8B  the cold walk that TS-17 compares against
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #455A64
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>Deriving a successor's shape summary</b>\nfrom the predecessor's summary, the mutation batch and the rewrite report

start
:predecessor summary <latex>(N, E, E_d, E_c, E_j, P, K)</latex>,\nthe mutation batch, and the rewrite report\nwith its mutation count, loaded <latex>\ell</latex> and placed <latex>p</latex>; <<#BBDEFB>>
if (the report's mutation count equals\nthe batch's entries in the three namespaces?) then (no)
  :refuse SemanticCoherence:\nthe report does not describe the batch; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:clone <latex>K</latex>, which shares its structure; <<#FFE0B2>>
while (an entry of namespace <latex>x</latex> remains,\ndata first, then continuations, then joins?) is (yes)
  if (its before-value exists?) then (yes)
    if (<latex>K</latex> holds the key's length?) then (no)
      :refuse SemanticCoherence:\na removed key length is absent; <<#FFCDD2>>
      stop
    else (yes)
      :release the length from <latex>K</latex>,\ncount one removal in <latex>R_x</latex>; <<#FFE0B2>>
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
  if (its after-value exists?) then (yes)
    :record the length in <latex>K</latex>,\ncount one addition in <latex>A_x</latex>; <<#FFE0B2>>
  else (no)
  endif
  if (<latex>x</latex> is the continuation map?) then (yes)
    :add <latex>\lVert r \rVert - 64</latex> for a present before-reference <latex>r</latex>\nto the removed payload, and for a present\nafter-reference to the added payload;\nrefuse ObjectLengthTooSmall below 64 bytes; <<#BBDEFB>>
  else (no)
  endif
endwhile (no)
:every total <latex>v</latex> becomes <latex>(v + \mathit{added}) - \mathit{removed}</latex>:\n<latex>N</latex> with <latex>p</latex> and <latex>\ell</latex>, <latex>E</latex> with the sums of <latex>A_x</latex> and <latex>R_x</latex>,\neach <latex>E_x</latex> with its own <latex>A_x</latex> and <latex>R_x</latex>, and <latex>P</latex> with the payloads; <<#BBDEFB>>
if (an addition overflows or a removal underflows?) then (yes)
  :refuse CounterOverflow or SemanticCoherence; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
:the successor summary <latex>(N', E', E'_d, E'_c, E'_j, P', K')</latex>;\nits maximum logical path <latex>M' = \max\left(K' \cup \{0\}\right)</latex>\nis the last length in big-endian order; <<#C8E6C9>>
stop

note right #ECEFF1
  <b>The check</b> (TS-17)
  The recording cold walk of the successor state
  counts the same totals and records each endpoint's
  key length once it validates. from_cold seeds a
  summary from that walk, refusing a multiset whose
  size or maximum differs from the walk's report.
  The derived summary must equal it field by field.
  ----
  <b>Why it is exact</b> (ExactStateShapeSummary.v)
  <latex>N(t) + \ell = N(s) + p</latex>, because every load removes
  one predecessor position and every placement creates
  one successor position; an admitted trie has no
  empty leaf, so <latex>M = \max\left(K \cup \{0\}\right)</latex>.
end note
@enduml
